#: passwords.cpp:40
msgid "Echo Characters As"
msgstr "Ego Karakters As"

#: passwords.cpp:42
msgid ""
"You can select the type of visual feedback given when you enter a password in "
"kdesu. Choose one of the following options:<p> <ul><li><em>1 star:</em> "
"each character you type is shown as an asterisk (*) symbol.</li> <li><em>"
"3 stars:</em> three asterisks are shown for each character you type.</li> <li>"
"<em>no echo:</em> there is no visual feedback at all, so nothing on your screen "
"shows how many characters are in your password.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""
"U kan kies die tipe van visuele terugvoer gegee wanneer u 'n wagwoord "
"in kdesu invoer. Kies een van die volgende opsies:<p> <ul><li><em>1 ster:</em> "
"elke karakter wat u tik word vertoon as 'n asterisk (*) simbool.</li> <li><em>"
"3 sterre:</em> drie sterretjie word vertoon vir elke karakter  wat u tik.</li> <li>"
"<em>geen ego:</em> daar is geen visuele terugvoer, sodat niks op u "
"skerm vertoon hoeveel karakters in u wagwoord is.</li></ul>"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid "&1 star"
msgstr "1 ster"

#: passwords.cpp:50
msgid "&3 stars"
msgstr "3 sterre"

#: passwords.cpp:51
msgid "&No echo"
msgstr "Geen ego"

#: passwords.cpp:56
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "Onthou wagwoorde"

#: passwords.cpp:57
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, kdesu will remember your passwords for the specified "
"amount of time. Until then, you will not have to enter your password again. "
"Keep in mind that this option is insecure and may enable others to damage your "
"system.<p> Please <em>do not</em> use this option if you are working in an "
"insecure environment, for example, on a workstation that is located in a "
"publicly accessible area.<p> This option does not affect passwords explicitly "
"set in other applications, for example, your email account password in KMail."
msgstr ""
"As hierdie opsie gemerk is, sal kdesu u wagwoord onthou vir die spesifiseerde "
"tydperk. Tot dan, sal die nie nodig wees om u wagwoord weer in te voer nie. "
"Neem kennis dat hierdie opsie onseker is en mag ander toelaat om u stelsel te beskadig. "
"<p> Asseblief <em>moenie</em> hierdie opsie gebruik as u in 'n onsekere omgewing "
"werk, byvoorbeeld, op 'n werkstasie wat in 'n publieke toeganklike area lokaliseer is. "
"<p> Hierdie opsie affekteer nie wagwoord eksplisiete instellings in ander aanwendings, "
"byvoorbeeld, u epos rekening wagwoord in Kpos."

#: passwords.cpp:70
msgid ""
"You can specify how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A short timeout is "
"more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"U kan spesifiseer hoe lank kdesu u wagwoorde moet onthou. 'n Kort "
"tydverstreke is meer beveilig as 'n lang tydverstreke."

#: passwords.cpp:73
msgid "&Timeout:"
msgstr "Tydverstreke:"

#: passwords.cpp:76
msgid " min"
msgstr " min"

#: passwords.cpp:189
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> This module gives you options for configuring the way in "
"which the \"kdesu\" program treats passwords. Kdesu will ask you for a password "
"when you try to carry out some privileged actions, such as changing the "
"date/time stored in your system clock, or adding new users on your computer.<p> "
"You can configure the type of visual feedback given when you type a password, "
"and whether kdesu should remember passwords for some time after you have given "
"them.<p> Note that these settings affect <em>only</em> "
"kdesu. This means that the behavior of passwords in KMail and other programs "
"cannot be configured here."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Wagwoorde</h1> Hierdie module gee u opsies vir konfigurering van die manier "
"waarop die \"kdesu\" program wagwoorde hanteer. Kdesu sal u vra na 'n "
"wagwoord wanneer u probeer sommige bevoorregde aksies uit te voer, soos die "
"verandering van die datum/tyd gestoor in u stelsel horlosie, of die toevoeging van nuwe "
"gebruikers op u rekenaar.<p> U kan die tipe van visuele terugvoer gegee "
"konfigureer wanneer u 'n wagwoord insleutel, en hetsy kdesu wagwoorde onthou moet word "
"vir 'n tyd nadat u het gegee het.<p> "
"Noteer dat hierdie instellings affekteer <em>slegs</em> "
"kdesu. Dit beteken dat die gedrag van wagwoorde in Kpos en ander programme "
"nie hier konfigureer kan word nie."

